WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.081
Minted

00:00:01.352 --> 00:00:03.085
a SwiftUI component

00:00:03.606 --> 00:00:04.407
Minted is a

00:00:04.219 --> 00:00:04.903
free

00:00:04.927 --> 00:00:06.789
MIT-licensed SwiftUI

00:00:06.601 --> 00:00:07.863
package that turns

00:00:07.745 --> 00:00:09.242
SVG paths or

00:00:09.054 --> 00:00:10.197
pin artwork into

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:10.940
physically lit

00:00:11.165 --> 00:00:12.473
spinning 3D gold

00:00:12.285 --> 00:00:13.723
medallions for achievement

00:00:13.535 --> 00:00:15.021
badges and commemorative

00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:15.445
coins

00:00:15.564 --> 00:00:16.778
with no 3D

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:17.544
model files

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.225
The post highlights

00:00:19.037 --> 00:00:20.110
four coin shapes

00:00:20.004 --> 00:00:21.277
engraved text and

00:00:21.089 --> 00:00:22.138
coins made from

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:22.739
images

00:00:22.878 --> 00:00:24.163
An ArtworkCoin mode

00:00:23.975 --> 00:00:25.248
traces the outline

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:25.956
of a finished

00:00:25.768 --> 00:00:26.982
pin image and

00:00:26.794 --> 00:00:27.878
renders its gold

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:28.739
as real metal

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:30.237
Per the README

00:00:30.473 --> 00:00:32.088
Minted generates geometry

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.326
from 2D paths

00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:34.800
adding enamel inlays

00:00:34.895 --> 00:00:36.203
studio reflections

00:00:36.015 --> 00:00:37.560
and momentum spins

00:00:38.094 --> 00:00:39.108
Full story on

00:00:38.919 --> 00:00:39.815
the dashboard
